A turn that is charged up to the count goes on owing from where it was charged before,
so the next charge takes the same counts again, and a thread that is charged often runs far less than its units;
a turn costs the counts it ran, once.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a step of the clock did not charge the thread whose turn it was its units' part
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -499,7 +499,6 @@ static uint64_t turn_charge(struct core *core)
     if (p != NULL) {
         p->vt = turn_vtime(core, p, now);
     }
-    core->turn_from = now;
     return now;
 }
 
